Apple Touch ID: accept SEP interface v4 and v5, so one build works on the
7.2 (v4) and 7.3 (v5) aurora kernels.

By Ryan Murray, from aurora-silicon/aurora-sep-userspace 12f26f61
(ae9e9323, 2026-10-31), libfprint/0005-aurora-support-v4-and-v5.patch, as
carried by aurora-silicon/alarm-aurora libfprint-aurora. LGPL-2.1-or-later,
like libfprint. Adapted only by name: SEP_BIO_* reads AURORA_BIO_* and
sep_bio_* reads aurora_bio_*, for this driver's aurora-bio.h.

Original description:

  aurora: support SEP v4 and v5 with versioned enrolment

  Keep existing v4 kernels usable while enabling v5 enrolment guards. Recheck
  GET_INFO at open, use the legacy v4 ioctl layout only on v4, and never retry
  a failed v5 request through the old interface. Matching uses the common ABI.

  Assisted-by: LLM
  Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>

